{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","id":"pg_a7b453ca334b5abbaacdb3d733183094","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/coderluii-holyclaude-docs-ollama-md-651c48fc01a9-b3d733183094.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_1b2a82dc771251619cd00677f8ed7f12"],"title":"CoderLuii/HolyClaude/docs/ollama.md @ 651c48fc01a9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_17cfd494612e019f235ee8c26ac4bb7241215c750aa4c0e5511885bf0e256f17"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Ollama is supported as an alternative to an Anthropic subscription via ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=ollama plus ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL pointing at the Ollama endpoint."},{"claim_ids":["clm_2b208af703c1309fb14678ddb1b7ef43ee00b56bbb84f4603add6d94b813f4e8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Environment variables are documented as all optional, covering timezone (TZ), UID/GID remapping (PUID/PGID), Node heap size, SMB polling flags, Apprise notification URLs (Discord, Telegram, Slack, email, etc.), and AI provider API keys."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4350ee935bbe2b417106246efadca148d48c44ccbad14fa9ae7377c5a1dd2b92"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Desloppify ships as a passive CLI in both images; it performs no scans or workspace edits unless invoked, and optional global skill setup at container start is controlled by HOLYCLAUDE_DESLOPPIFY_SETUP with values like off, claude, codex, gemini, all, or opencode (full image only)."},{"claim_ids":["clm_59ddcfbeb481916d3b6946b5013ee2b96a275f36e1180002e410367686d3a887"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Authentication is done through the CloudCLI web UI: Claude Max/Pro users sign in via OAuth and API-key users paste their key; the container relays no credentials, with tools reading them from container files, bind mounts, or environment variables."},{"claim_ids":["clm_5e6130c76f958b181253973a2144dcad524b001dad5c6d3229d075ef86daa7fb"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The compose templates set shm_size 2g because Chromium heavily uses /dev/shm and Docker's 64MB default causes tab crashes, and grant SYS_ADMIN, SYS_PTRACE, and seccomp=unconfined as the retained browser profile, with hardening described as a separate change."},{"claim_ids":["clm_834c894ec4750c146a70875c9668e9f65d391410dc5fa087059421ce06d2e324"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"OpenAI API keys cannot authenticate Claude Code; they work with the bundled Codex CLI instead, and ChatGPT Plus/Pro subscribers authenticate Codex via codex login --device-auth, optionally exposing port 1455 for the browser callback flow."},{"claim_ids":["clm_996a0de973fd74e5a31437dedd19160c5089ba00a1795d1bfc807932414257ac"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Persistence is via bind mounts: ./data/claude maps to /home/claude/.claude (holding settings, credentials, and Claude's memory) and ./workspace maps to /workspace; on every boot Git/gh config is linked into the .claude mount, and bootstrap.sh copies defaults only on first boot, marking it with .holyclaude-bootstrapped."},{"claim_ids":["clm_adb2dd625e4f4f78c5bf22b20786152810090a2ae97a76e0d5a48d73361732f5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The image bundles Chromium with Xvfb and Playwright for headless browser screenshots and testing, plus database clients (psql, redis-cli, sqlite3, MariaDB-based mysql) and GitHub CLI."},{"claim_ids":["clm_ba4eb6720683133398e9d74a0b7448d09ffb76f5cf15343d24c31930336d01d4"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The full image ships eight AI CLIs — Claude Code, Gemini, Codex, Cursor, TaskMaster, Junie, OpenCode, and Pi — while the slim image ships the five core ones (Claude Code, Gemini, Codex, Cursor, TaskMaster), with slim installing missing tools on demand."},{"claim_ids":["clm_c0254316595719bf4d7309a6333c3b2ad47fd4d18192cf89ce16862df5350254"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The container runs the official Anthropic Claude Code CLI (not a wrapper or proxy), served through a CloudCLI web UI on port 3001, with s6-overlay as PID 1 supervising Xvfb on :99 and optional sshd."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d15804f92f7e1ee1bba4295ee9384bad14f7e4e4b819f430e2e1cc1a7d398bc5"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The quick-start workflow is: create a docker-compose.yaml from a provided template, run docker compose up -d, then open http://localhost:3001 and create a CloudCLI account; no .env file is required."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e3f3cc373802532e8d253e4bc5de229305fe7150ec357f3d2b6b34787a9dcb4d"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The web UI port is bound to 127.0.0.1 by default, and users needing remote access are directed to Tailscale or Cloudflare Tunnel rather than port forwarding."},{"claim_ids":["clm_efbd9e32c74522b076cb6d5e75c71d85b485f5c9fc709f8e340aa7664e2cd9e7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: release-sensitive facts are published in contracts/product-facts.json, and the release workflow checks that contract against the Dockerfile and Compose files before building images."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f84a68605642efca20febf07e64953adaa33b80fd95f29ace6b5e951a4219855"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Two image variants are published on Docker Hub: latest (full, everything pre-installed) and slim (core tools only, with Claude installing extras on demand), plus pinned X.Y.Z and X.Y.Z-slim tags for production stability."}],"claim_ids":["clm_17cfd494612e019f235ee8c26ac4bb7241215c750aa4c0e5511885bf0e256f17","clm_2b208af703c1309fb14678ddb1b7ef43ee00b56bbb84f4603add6d94b813f4e8","clm_4350ee935bbe2b417106246efadca148d48c44ccbad14fa9ae7377c5a1dd2b92","clm_59ddcfbeb481916d3b6946b5013ee2b96a275f36e1180002e410367686d3a887","clm_5e6130c76f958b181253973a2144dcad524b001dad5c6d3229d075ef86daa7fb","clm_834c894ec4750c146a70875c9668e9f65d391410dc5fa087059421ce06d2e324","clm_996a0de973fd74e5a31437dedd19160c5089ba00a1795d1bfc807932414257ac","clm_adb2dd625e4f4f78c5bf22b20786152810090a2ae97a76e0d5a48d73361732f5","clm_ba4eb6720683133398e9d74a0b7448d09ffb76f5cf15343d24c31930336d01d4","clm_c0254316595719bf4d7309a6333c3b2ad47fd4d18192cf89ce16862df5350254","clm_d15804f92f7e1ee1bba4295ee9384bad14f7e4e4b819f430e2e1cc1a7d398bc5","clm_e3f3cc373802532e8d253e4bc5de229305fe7150ec357f3d2b6b34787a9dcb4d","clm_efbd9e32c74522b076cb6d5e75c71d85b485f5c9fc709f8e340aa7664e2cd9e7","clm_f84a68605642efca20febf07e64953adaa33b80fd95f29ace6b5e951a4219855"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","created_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833","id":"pg_af2daa3a8ac45dcf9b10db2f0f31cd21","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/coderluii-holyclaude-readme-md-651c48fc01a9-db2f0f31cd21.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_980bbb35c5665b17a699fd87bef01b62"],"title":"CoderLuii/HolyClaude/README.md @ 651c48fc01a9","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:42:12Z","updated_by_operation":"op_f88a06e10bb9453bb6bb0edfd51b3833"}
